## Check results

- `./config/pi/build-agents.sh --check`: `OK: AGENTS/CLAUDE files match fragments`.
- `./config/pi/verify.sh`: four of the five failures are symlinks on this eval home that don't point at this repo: `~/.pi/agent/bin`, `web-search.json`, `~/.config/git/template` and the worktrunk `config.toml`.
- The fifth is `node tests pass`: 148 of 157 pass. All 9 failures are the herdr pane tests in `scout-bin.test.ts`. A copy of `HEAD` fails the same 9, plus one worker test that has since been deleted.
- tsc was skipped because it isn't installed here.

## Found

- `slice-check` will flag `tests/slice-check.test.ts` itself for "new skip/only/todo markers", because its fixtures contain `test.skip(` and `test.only(`. That's a known false positive of the text heuristic.
- After you pull this into the live dotfiles, these links will point at deleted files: `~/.config/husky/init.sh`, plus `~/.local/bin/auto-guard` if it exists there. Existing repos' hook lines call `auto-guard` behind `command -v`, so they stop running quietly. Remove the links by hand.
- `DESIGN.md` Activation still says `install.sh` links `agents/`, which was already wrong before this change.